{"@context":{"@vocab":"https://tacitus.me/ns/reference#"},"@graph":[{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:ceasefire","@type":"Process","label":"Proposed nationwide ceasefire"},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:governance","@type":"Process","label":"Proposed governance and election process"},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:talks","@type":"Process","label":"Proposed formal negotiations"},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:unsc","@type":"Institution","label":"UN Security Council"},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:source:eb0f5db7d5fdffe93efeb041ea85b1f38564c3fe2911733ae7d06ffe6c7ad201","@type":"Source","label":"Security Council resolution 2254 (2015)","url":"https://documents.un.org/doc/undoc/gen/n15/443/34/pdf/n1544334.pdf","version":"69c6305fe434a4b180a95de44fad4b6262f21395dd41f45ea235e36331774689"},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:statement:ceasefire-link","@type":"Statement","cites":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:evidence:ceasefire-link"},"label":"The Council linked its support for a ceasefire to initial political-transition steps; this is not a finding of a nationwide ceasefire.","modality":"expressed_support","object":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:ceasefire"},"predicate":"normative_position","qualifiedBy":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:ceasefire-link:0"},"qualifiers_json":"[{\"end\":501,\"start\":353,\"text\":\"as soon as the representatives of the Syrian government and the opposition have begun initial steps towards a political transition under UN auspices\"}]","review_state":"proposed","subject":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:unsc"}},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:evidence:ceasefire-link","@type":"EvidenceSpan","end":1821,"fromSource":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:source:eb0f5db7d5fdffe93efeb041ea85b1f38564c3fe2911733ae7d06ffe6c7ad201"},"offset_unit":"unicode_codepoints","quote":"5. Acknowledges the close linkage between a ceasefire and a parallel political process, pursuant to the 2012 Geneva Communiqué, and that both initiatives should move ahead expeditiously, and in this regard expresses its support for a nationwide ceasefire in Syria, which the ISSG has committed to support and assist in implementing, to come into effect as soon as the representatives of the Syrian government and the opposition have begun initial steps towards a political transition under UN auspices, on the basis of the Geneva Communiqué, as set forth in the 14 November 2015 ISSG Statement, and to do so on an urgent basis;","start":1194},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:ceasefire-link:0","@type":"Qualification","label":"as soon as the representatives of the Syrian government and the opposition have begun initial steps towards a political transition under UN auspices","review_state":"proposed","source_end":1695,"source_start":1547},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:statement:convene-talks","@type":"Statement","cites":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:evidence:convene-talks"},"label":"The Council requested convening negotiations with a historical target; the text does not establish that talks occurred.","modality":"requested","object":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:talks"},"predicate":"normative_position","qualifiedBy":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:convene-talks:0"},"qualifiers_json":"[{\"end\":301,\"start\":266,\"text\":\"with a target of early January 2016\"}]","review_state":"proposed","subject":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:unsc"}},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:evidence:convene-talks","@type":"EvidenceSpan","end":479,"fromSource":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:source:eb0f5db7d5fdffe93efeb041ea85b1f38564c3fe2911733ae7d06ffe6c7ad201"},"offset_unit":"unicode_codepoints","quote":"2. Requests the Secretary-General, through his good offices and the efforts of his Special Envoy for Syria, to convene representatives of the Syrian government and the opposition to engage in formal negotiations on a political transition process on an urgent basis, with a target of early January 2016 for the initiation of talks, pursuant to the Geneva Communiqué, consistent with the 14 November 2015 ISSG Statement, with a view to a lasting political settlement of the crisis;","start":0},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:convene-talks:0","@type":"Qualification","label":"with a target of early January 2016","review_state":"proposed","source_end":301,"source_start":266},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:statement:governance-process","@type":"Statement","cites":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:evidence:governance-process"},"label":"The Council expressed support for an inclusive political process and historical election timetable; this is not an implementation finding.","modality":"expressed_support","object":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:governance"},"predicate":"normative_position","qualifiedBy":[{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:governance-process:0"},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:governance-process:1"}],"qualifiers_json":"[{\"end\":153,\"start\":124,\"text\":\"within a target of six months\"},{\"end\":376,\"start\":344,\"text\":\"pursuant to the new constitution\"}]","review_state":"proposed","subject":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:entity:unsc"}},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:evidence:governance-process","@type":"EvidenceSpan","end":1192,"fromSource":{"@id":"urn:tacitus:source:eb0f5db7d5fdffe93efeb041ea85b1f38564c3fe2911733ae7d06ffe6c7ad201"},"offset_unit":"unicode_codepoints","quote":"4. Expresses its support, in this regard, for a Syrian-led political process that is facilitated by the United Nations and, within a target of six months, establishes credible, inclusive and non-sectarian governance and sets a schedule and process for drafting a new constitution, and further expresses its support for free and fair elections, pursuant to the new constitution, to be held within 18 months and administered under supervision of the United Nations, to the satisfaction of the governance and to the highest international standards of transparency and accountability, with all Syrians, including members of the diaspora, eligible to participate, as set forth in the 14 November 2015 ISSG Statement;","start":481},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:governance-process:0","@type":"Qualification","label":"within a target of six months","review_state":"proposed","source_end":634,"source_start":605},{"@id":"urn:tacitus:qualification:governance-process:1","@type":"Qualification","label":"pursuant to the new constitution","review_state":"proposed","source_end":857,"source_start":825}]}
